      "readmeSignals": {
        "title": null,
        "summary": "Persistent memory compression system built for Claude Code . Quick Start • How It Works • Search Tools • Documentation • Configuration • Troubleshooting • License Claude-Mem seamlessly preserves context across sessions by automatically capturing tool usage observations, generating semantic summaries, and making them available to future sessions. This enables Claude to maintain continuity of knowledge about projects even after sessions end or reconnect. Grok Bot has no host hooks, so we watch the chat log files. Default is CMEM Pro, the hosted memory. Local observer is opt-in: --provider host. Installing this plugin does not install Cursor.",
